   "reproduction": {
    "command": "registerCredential('ADJ_TEST','FAIL xy'); ciSignature('test','setup\\nFAIL xy\\nend','failure') run against head and against a git-archive copy of base under $TMPDIR/adj",
    "output": "head: {\"line\":\"FAIL xy\",\"signature\":\"[\\\"test\\\",\\\"FAIL xy\\\",null]\",\"excerpt\":\"setup\\nFAIL xy\\nend\"}; base: {\"line\":\"[redacted]\",\"signature\":\"[\\\"test\\\",\\\"[redacted]\\\",null]\"}"
   },
   "evidence": "Base: `const bounded = (text) => redactCredentials(text).trim().slice(0, 500)` was applied to the single line, so redactText's `text === secret` exact-match branch fired for short secrets. Head: `bounded` calls `publication(text, from, to)`, which redacts `text.slice(start, to + padding)`: a window padded with neighbouring characters that never equals the credential. Then `redactText`'s `if (substring || text === secret)` skips short variants. `Store.recordCiFailure` saves `f.signature` and `f.line` without redacting them."
  }
